["In the medulla, the medial lemniscus stands vertically along the midline ('feet ventral, cervical/arms dorsal'); in the midbrain, it rotates horizontally ('feet lateral, arms/cervical medial')", "In the medulla, feet are medial; in the midbrain, feet are anterior", "In both medulla and midbrain, feet are always dorsal and arms are ventral", "In the medulla, feet are lateral; in the midbrain, feet are medial", "The medial lemniscus has no somatotopic organization until reaching the thalamus"],
